[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:96. The Dead Return]
[00:00.440]Passage 96 | 文章九十六
[00:02.825]The Dead Return. | 死者归来。
[00:07.820]A festival for the dead is held once a year in Japan. | 日本每年举行一次祭奠亡灵的节日。
[00:13.055]This festival is a cheerful occasion. | 这个节日是一个欢乐的时刻。
[00:16.775]For on this day, the dead are said to return to their homes, | 因为在这一天，据说亡灵会回到他们的家园，
[00:21.395]and they are welcomed by the living. | 并受到生者的欢迎。
[00:24.725]As they are expected to be hungry after their long journey, | 由于他们经过长途跋涉，预计会很饥饿，
[00:29.825]food is laid out for them. | 所以为他们准备了食物。
[00:32.960]Specially made lanterns are hung outside each house | 特制的灯笼挂在每家每户的外面，
[00:37.765]to help the dead to find their way. | 以帮助亡灵找到回家的路。
[00:40.885]All night long, people dance and sing. | 整夜，人们都在跳舞唱歌。
[00:45.835]In the early morning, the food that had been laid out for the dead | 清晨，为亡灵准备的食物，
[00:51.260]is thrown into a river or into the sea, | 被扔进河里或海里，
[00:54.500]as it is considered unlucky for anyone living to eat it. | 因为生者食用这些食物被认为是不吉利的。
[01:00.105]In towns that are near the sea, | 在靠近大海的城镇，
[01:03.215]the tiny lanterns, which had been hung in the streets the night before, | 前一晚挂在街上的小灯笼，
[01:07.430]are placed into the water when the festival is over. | 在节日结束后被放入水中。
[01:11.890]Thousands of lanterns slowly drift out to sea, | 成千上万的灯笼慢慢地漂向大海，
[01:16.920]guiding the dead on their return journey to the other world. | 指引着亡灵返回另一个世界。
[01:22.530]This is a moving spectacle, | 这是一个感人的景象，
[01:25.570]for crowds of people stand on the shore, | 因为成群结队的人们站在岸边，
[01:28.730]watching the lanterns drifting away | 看着灯笼渐渐远去，
[01:31.850]until they can be seen no more. | 直到它们再也看不见。